  "title": "Ali K NDE 4229",
  "date": "6.6.2009",
  "content": "I departed from Istanbul to Giresun to visit my parent's graves. When I arrived, I started to sweat and I had back pain. I called my brother with my cell phone and told him my condition. I was taxied to the village clinic in Görele. Afterward, I was transported to the city clinic in Giresun. When I arrived at the clinic, I was conscious and soaked with sweat. They brought me with a stretcher into the emergency room and I started to see my surroundings darker. They thought my blood pressure dropped. I started to shake and I felt my arms were very weak. I cannot remember further. When I was conscious again, a nurse told me my heartbeat stopped twice and the doctors had to electroshock me to bring me back to life. I told this because when my heartbeat stopped, I was in a kind of a tunnel. I was on my knees, naked, my elbow on my knee, my head rested in my hand. I was thinking. I watched the 'me' in the tunnel from two to three meters distance from above. When I looked at myself I saw at the end of the tunnel a place with yellowish colorful mist at the sky, which illuminated the place like a sun illuminates the days and this light shined into the tunnel.",
